WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.520
Speaker 1: OK, next question is very related
to the first one.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:10.620
Are the college educated white voters actually
becoming more liberal?

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:14.680
There's a very interesting dynamic that's
going on here with college educated whites

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:21.700
I talk to you must have been about a month
ago about the abandonment among some of the

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:26.910
Republican Party moving to the Democratic
Party or moving to be independents who still

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:30.220
may vote for Republicans or whatever the case
may be.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:36.820
It is absolutely true that this has been a
shift over time among college educated white

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:37.820
voters.

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:43.100
College educated white voters some decades
ago leaned much more to the right, and it

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.410
was primarily for economic reasons.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:51.940
The idea and this came up during the voicemail
segment on Monday, the idea being college

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:57.180
educated people are more likely to make more
money and they want to keep the money.

00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:00.690
So they vote for Republicans because they
see Republicans as keeping their taxes low.

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:03.700
And that's a very nice, concise little explanation.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:09.020
And certainly some decades ago, there was
probably a lot of truth to that.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:15.009
However, we've now seen more college educated
whites over time move in the direction of

00:01:15.009 --> 00:01:16.649
voting for more and more Democrats.

00:01:16.649 --> 00:01:18.979
I think that there are two things going on
here.

00:01:18.979 --> 00:01:26.210
Number one, although the Republican Party
is still seen widely as the low tax party,

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:29.389
the daylight between the two parties has gotten
smaller and smaller.

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:32.649
Now, I know Joe Biden now is talking about
doubling the capital gains rate on people

00:01:32.649 --> 00:01:34.829
making over a million dollars in all these
different things.

00:01:34.829 --> 00:01:38.049
But the vast majority of people don't make
over a million dollars.

00:01:38.049 --> 00:01:43.529
And so when you think about college educated
Democrats or college educated voters making

00:01:43.529 --> 00:01:49.380
between 80 and one hundred and eighty thousand
dollars or something like that, they may actually

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:55.279
be realizing, you know, the very small difference
in what I might pay in taxes under the Republican

00:01:55.279 --> 00:02:03.069
versus Democratic plans is not enough to override
all the other reasons that the college educated

00:02:03.069 --> 00:02:05.369
white voter has been moving to the left.

00:02:05.369 --> 00:02:08.640
And this includes social issues.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:12.130
This includes cultural elements as well.

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:18.660
So while the economics are always reflexively
what we might go to, social attitudes have

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:19.660
changed as well.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:24.390
I mean, look at something like approval of
Black Lives Matter in 2017.

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:29.220
If you polled white college graduates, do
you support Black Lives Matter?

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:31.810
Twenty nine percent said, yes, I do.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:38.950
That same poll right now has 40 percent of
white college graduates supporting Black Lives

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:40.050
Matter.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:42.870
That's an increase of almost thirty three
percent.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:43.870
Remember, not 30.

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:50.850
It's 11 percentage points, but about almost
a third, about 30 percent that it appears

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:53.680
significantly overrides.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:59.500
The top tax bracket is three points lower
under the Republican plan.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:08.100
And so that to me, seems like a major factor
in what we've seen from college educated white

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:12.790
voters moving more to the Democratic Party.

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:19.040
The other thing also that may be going on
is that as people simply become more politically

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:26.470
aware, they make more rational decisions about
where they say they align before.

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:33.200
One of the things that Trump did and we saw
it in absolute record turnout in twenty twenty

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:37.650
Trump getting way more votes than he got in
2016, Biden getting way more votes than anyone

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.890
has gotten.

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:45.560
So one of the things that we saw Trump do,
for better or worse, is engage a lot of new

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:46.780
people.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:53.740
And there are likely lots of college educated
white voters who are recently out of college

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:59.110
who were in some nominal way kind of following
the politics of their parents.

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:03.300
Maybe maybe you maybe had some really, you
know, twenty one twenty two twenty year old

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:10.360
in college or college graduates that in 2015
were Republicans in some nominal way, but

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:14.650
maybe they didn't vote, for example, as they
became more politically aware.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:18.799
I'm not using the term WOAK, but as they became
more engaged in politics during the Trump

00:04:18.799 --> 00:04:20.959
era and they more understood.

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:21.959
Oh, wait a second.

00:04:21.959 --> 00:04:25.389
Yeah, I don't know what my parents saw in
the Republican Party, but I don't see it with

00:04:25.389 --> 00:04:26.389
Trump.

00:04:26.389 --> 00:04:28.629
I'm going to become a Democrat, for example.

00:04:28.629 --> 00:04:34.819
I think that that's a factor as well, that
sometimes you just have people who more as

00:04:34.819 --> 00:04:38.729
they get more involved, they understand that
whatever they were nominally identifying with

00:04:38.729 --> 00:04:40.520
originally really wasn't for them.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:43.419
And so that may be something you see in the
numbers.

00:04:43.419 --> 00:04:48.240
That may not not actually reflect the shift,
it may simply reflect a change from not paying

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:51.599
attention to paying attention, some things
to think about.

00:04:51.599 --> 00:04:52.599
Let me know your thoughts on this.

00:04:52.599 --> 00:04:52.603
One last question today,

